{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.context State.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.context State.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bpy.context state bpy.context state","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.context State.md","fileName":"bpy.context State.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"bpy.context State","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Python Data and Operations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Data and Operations","Blender Object Lookup by Name","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.context State.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.context State.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bpy.context state bpy.context state","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.context State.md","fileName":"bpy.context State.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"bpy.context State","heading":"bpy.context State","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"`bpy.context` exposes the state in which a Blender operation is evaluated. It can identify the scene, mode, selected objects, active object, and data associated with the current interface area. Operator behavior often changes or becomes unavailable when this state does not meet its requirements.\n\nContext is a convenient path to what the user is currently working with, but it is not a permanent identity for that data. When a script needs a particular object regardless of interface focus, [[Blender Object Lookup by Name]] through `bpy.data` makes that dependency explicit.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Data and Operations","Blender Object Lookup by Name","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.context State.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/bpy.context